2 CONT October 19, 1617 = '''Volpert Schulte zum Lohe and Anna''' his wife sell part of their farm to the master tailor Balthasar Stirnberg and his wife Magdalene zu Reiste. The ancestors of the sellers acquired the same farms from the B
2 CONC leffken zu Reiste and had hereditary possession from time immemorial up to this point.''' Volpert Lohmann''' asks his''' cousin Hermann von Marpe gt. Pape''', court clerk, to seal the letter and '''to sign next to him and his son 
2 CONC Jobsten.''' (Certificate, in the Reiste parish archive)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 11/12/1626 = Hermann Rumpff the Younger to Wenne enfeoffed''' Hermann Schulte gt. Lohmann''' on behalf of and because of his underage step-son Hermann Lomann with his entertaining good and his justice except the Share of the job f
2 CONC rom Oill (Münster State Archives, feudal files)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 07/03/1638 = '''Ebert Schulte zu Landenbeck''' commits himself to good things as liege lord to the Struwen Büemke the interest from both the 5 Rtlr., As well as of the 5 Rtlr. To pay Maria Stoer'sche memorial money, if Struwen sho
2 CONC uld stay behind. He pledged the Wiesenkamp behind the Büemke chapel adjoins Cordes Kamp. Witnesses: Pastor Caspar Berghoff, Hermann Lohmann, Thonies Scheiwe, both lay judges and provisional officers. Signature: Eberdt Schulte to l
2 CONC amb corner. (From a booklet with copies of old documents in the parish archive of Reiste, pages 15-16)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT July 16, 1638 = Lambert Plett zu Beisinghausen and his wife Maria confess that '''Hermann Lohmann and his wife Agnes''' their chairman Johannes Plett 20 Rtlr. have borrowed. (Copy of the document in the Bernhard Greiff estate)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 02/28/1640 = Pastor Caspar Berghoff zu traveled to Thonies Scheiwe with his provisional agents Erflinghausen and Rottger Schulte zu Reiste sell the dean with permission Theodor Verheiden zu Meschede a pastorate above the Stakelbra
2 CONC ucks, in front of''' Hermann Lohmanns''' Lands, beniden out "on Beckers Land, above Plete Land, '''the owner of the Lohof Hermann Lohmann'''. The purchase price is subject to interest created by Heinrich Hellermann zu Beisinghause
2 CONC n. Signatures: Lammert Pleit, Beisinghausen, Eberdt Schulte zu Lammecke, Rötger Stirnberg zu Reiste. (Document in the Reiste parish archive)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 08/13/1641 = Jobst Cordes (zu Büemke) confesses that he was given by '''Hermann Lohmann to Loe''', Court shepherd and Röttger Stirnberg in these troubled and protracted wars. times and in his greatest needs 20 Rtlr. have borrowed.
2 CONC  (Meschede State Archives, Meschede Monastery, documents)
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 04/30/1645 = '''Hermann Lohmann and "Joanna his sister-in-law von Ennest''' are godparents Hermann Roggemann zu Niederreiste. (Church book in the Reiste parish archive)
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 08/10/1648 = '''Hermannus Lohmann''' is godfather to Hermann Gerwen, son of Evert, in Arpe Gerwen and Gertrud Schulte zu Kückelheim. (Church book in the Berghausen parish archive)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 09/30/1648 (Sunday after Michaelis) =''' Hermann Lohmann the elder takes care of the housekeeping Left the Lohof to his stepson Hermann Lohmann, the younger.''' (See the copy of the certificate from May 10th, 1664 at the Lohofe)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 05/17/1652 =''' Hermann Lohmann becomes a Fredeburg castle fief''' with the Lohof which the von Ohl zu Lehn received and had earlier, from Maximilian Heinrich, Archbishop of Cologne, enfeoffed. Witnesses: The council and head wait
2 CONC er in Arnsberg Johen Clouth and Herman Dunker. (Original parchment certificate in the Reiste parish archive.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 09.11.1652 = Adam Diethrich Rumpf zur Wenne enfeoffs '''Hermann Lohmann zu Lohof''' im Parish Traveled with the estate (Lohof) under his control, except for the part the good that Oill received from the Elector of Cologne at Lehn,
2 CONC  but Lohmann as Pledge. (Münster State Archives, State Archives, copy by Hermann Pape)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 18.09.1653 = Dieddrich and Elisabeth Schmidts von Reiste, brother and sister, sell with the knowledge of her former guardian Jobst Hanen, sexton to Calle, her estate to traveled, called Schmidts Gut zu Reiste to Röttger Stirnberg 
2 CONC and Catharina his housewife. You ask the electoral judge Jacob Scheffer of the Eslohe and Reiste courts Seal letter. Witnesses: Hermann Rumpff zur Wenne, Elector Droste zu Stadtberge and Volkmarsen, '''Hermann Lomann, judicial off
2 CONC icer''', Hermann Baust, Jobsten Hanen to Calle. Signatures: Jacob Scheffer, judge, Hermann Pape, magistrate. (Original parchment certificate in the parish archive of Reiste, see also: Certificate from 01/27/1659)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 26.08.1658 = The brothers Eberhard, Jost and Caspar Frisse von Reiste confess that they H'''ermann Lohmann, electoral court clerk in Eslohe, their parents' home''' to traveled with all countries, etc., for a sum of money which the
2 CONC  Buyers have to pay their parents and forefathers, creditors, on themselves. You ask to seal the letter to the electoral judge in Eslohe. Signatures: Jacob Schefer (from Grevenstein), electoral judge at Eslohe, Ebert Schulte zu La
2 CONC ndenbeck, Hermann Lohmann, court assistant. (Original parchment certificate from Kanter-Frisse zu Reiste) NB 1659, '''Thonies Lohmann, the son of Hermann Lohmann, married Frissen-Hof zu Traveled'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 01/27/1659 = Dietrich Schmidt von Reiste, Everhardt Kramer, Schöffe zu Wallen, Else Schmidt, his housewife, selling her parental blacksmith's property with all pertinents and inside and outside of Reiste accessories to the honorab
2 CONC le Rötger Stirnberg gt. Balthes too traveled. The rest of the purchase price has been paid. Signed notary Hermann Pape to Marpe. Witnesses Hermann Rumpff to Wenne and Reiste, Fbert Schulte to Langenbeck, magistrate,''' Hermann Loh
2 CONC mann, magistrate'''. (Document in the parish archive of Reiste) See also the document dated September 18, 1653.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 06.02.1662 = Jacob Schotter zu Grevenstein, Richter zu Eslohe and Reiste and the '''Judges Hermann Lohmann''' and Jürgen Spekenhöver are witnesses to one The couple Ernst Jost Schledorn and Theodora Guida von Neuhof are sold to th
2 CONC eirs Neighbors and "godfather" Hermann Pape, clerk at Eslohe and Schliprüthen (Dornseiffer, Joh., Geschichtlichen über Eslohe, Paderborn, 1896, p. 36)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT May 10th, 1644 = '''Hermann Lohmann the Elder''' writes to the electoral councilors of Arnsberg '''His stepson Hermann Lohmann zum Lohoff,''' whom he received on Sunday after Michaelis in 1648 Handed over the housekeeping, came hi
2 CONC s then assumed obligation not after him. On March 22nd, 1659 there was already a judgment in Eslohe against this happened to his stepson. Please now the Electoral Chancellery, gentlemen Seriously urging judges in Eslohe and Reiste
2 CONC  to carry out the judgment. Therefore the decision is issued by Arnsberg under the above date. (Copy of the certificate at the Lohhof)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1665 = Copy of a complaint by '''Hermann Lohmann, the elder, to Reiste''' against''' his Stepson''' of the same name at the Lohof on payment of his old age pension. (Copy of the document - badly damaged by mice - on the Lohof)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 01/28/1666 = Dietrich and Johann Weber zu Beisinghausen, father and son, Elisabeth and Anna, whose housewives declare that they are the elector's court clerk Hermann Lehmann and his wife Margarethe lift the share of a mountain sol
2 CONC d. Sealer: Hermann Pape zu Marpe, Richter zu Eslohe and Reiste. (Document in the Reiste parish archive)
2 CONT
2 CONT 01/30/1666 = '''Hermann Lohmann, the elder, to (Lohof bei) Reiste''' complains again to the electoral office of Arneberg against "Hermann Lohmann zum Lohof, my Stepson ". In response to the lawsuit of May 10, 1664, a settlement wa
2 CONC s made on June 29 of the same Year (= 29.06.1664) came about, in which the stepson is handwritten I am obliged to deliver 9 bushels of rye and 9 bushels of barley to him annually once 70 Rtlr. to pay. He only gave the grain for 1 
2 CONC year, "not of the money." the least ". So he asked again to instruct the judge in Eslohe, now to proceed to execution. The law firm zu Arnsberg (Joannes Wordehoff, Landschreiber): "So we are not responsible for what we have compar
2 CONC ed to different times and what to do theill by the last transaction confirmirt andt confirmed andt to prestire and pay, As if the electoral judge was committed to Esloh, the defendant Lohman time of 14 days to amicable payment of 
2 CONC both the promised annual grain and different money .... (to be stopped?), otherwise he should get execution to let. Arnspergh, date as above. " (Old copy of the certificate (badly damaged by mouse eating) on the Lohof)
2 CONT
2 CONT July 8th, 1667 = Röttger Stirnberg and Catharina Balthes zu Reiste, married couple, declare that they will bequeath their Balthes dwelling with living and dead inventory to the honorable and virtuous Elisabeth Fredebolinges for ma
2 CONC ny years of loyal service. They ask Hermann and Toniesen Lomann, father and son, Everhardt Schulte zu Landenbeck, the judge zu Eslohe and Reiste Jacob Scheffer to sign and seal the letter of purchase. Signatures: Jacobus Scheffer,
2 CONC  Caspar (Stirnberg gt.) Baltz, for me and my housewives, '''Hermann Lomann, magistrate''', Ebert Schulte (from Landenbeck), I confess Tonies Lohmann to me and Catrina my married housewife that this is true. (Original certificate a
2 CONC t the Lohof)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
