2 CONC ''',+ vor 1637 ?); II. Reiste 22.11.1637 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lohmann, Elsken''', * Reiste um 1615, + Reisinghausen (Pf. Reiste) 14.4.1686 'plena dierum et virtutis et probitatis dum vixit uxor in aedibus Boestes' ‘Voller Mut und Ehrlichkeit der Tage, als seine Frau im Böstes Hof zu Beisi
2 CONC nghausen (Haus Boeste) lebte'
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hermann Schelmann ca 1610- -Niederberndorf. Deceased 26 December 1656 - Beisinghausen''', aged about 46 years old1656.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of '''Heinrich Baust (around 1585 - after 1627)''', Hermann Schelmann from Niederberndorf appears as heir to the court. Either '''Heinrich Baust's''' marriage was now childless and Hermann Schelmann was installed a
2 CONC s heir, or: '''Heinrich Baust was born in Niederberndorf and married the heir's daughter in Beisinghausen.''' From the scant documentary material, something more precise cannot be ascertained ... 1648 = Boss tho Bosinghausen belon
2 CONC gs to the farms owned by Schulte zu Landenbeck (State Archives Miinster, Stift Meschede, I.ehnsarchiv, files 5a)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 04.01.1682 = "Jch '''Elsa Lohmann Wittibe Herman Boiste''' säl. Zu Bösinghausen announce and I hereby confess to me, my children and descendants, that my '''dear brother Herman Lohman, electoral bailiff,''' itziger owner who gave 
2 CONC Lohoffe "..... Properly paid for marriage property and child part from the Lohof. Witnesses: Volpert Klopper and Johannes Plett zu Beisinghausen Signatures: Jodokus Molitor "ex Päbstl. Undt Kayserl. makes open notary (to Bremke) I
2 CONC , Johannes Baust, quit before my mother. (Files on the Lohof)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 04.10.1662	the '''Lohmann siblings''' from Reiste are suing for '''themselves''' and their '''sister's daughter Clara against '''Ebert Schulte from Landenbeck,''' who is said to have said on 04.10.1662 during Bauste's break in Bei
2 CONC singhausen: '''His son's wife had come from the devil; she doesn't want to give him anything to eat''' (Original paper certificate at the Lohof). '''The lawsuit was filed on Elsen Baustes to Beisinghausen'''
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 1663 = Johannes Lohmann, priest and conventual of the Grafschaft monastery, Hermann Lohmann the younger to Lohof, Thonis Lohmann to Reiste,''' Elsen Baustes to Beisinghausen''', Gertrud Möller'sche zu Fretter, all biological broth
2 CONC ers and sisters, complain for themselves and Clara her sister daughter against '''Ebert Schulte zu Landenbeck''' for insulting. He should be on Sunday, October 4th, 1662, in Baustes house in Beisinghausen in the presence of others
2 CONC  have said that his son's wife came from the devil; she doesn't want him anything to eat. (Original paper certificate at the Lohof) His son's wife was Clara Lohmann, who gave. around 1630, + Landenbeck 06/10/1677. Man remember tha
2 CONC t this utterance has fallen to the witch frenzy at the moment and it is easy to become one Persecution through the (witch) courts could come. That's why they complain. Siblings of Clara Lohmann.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Clara Lohman aka Clara Baust''' married '''son(NN) of Ebert Schulte zu Landenbeck'''. Her father and mother was '''Hermann Schelmann gnt. Baust ca 1610-1656 and Elisabeth Lohmann ca 1620-1686.''' After the death of '''Heinrich 
2 CONC Baust (around 1585 - after 1627), Hermann Schelmann from Niederberndorf appears as heir to the court. Either Heinrich Baust's marriage was now childless and Hermann Schelmann was installed as heir, or: Heinrich Baust was born in N
2 CONC iederberndorf and married the heir's daughter in Beisinghausen.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Familienseite: Familienseite
2 CONT
