1 NOTE {geni:about_me} July 8th, 1667 = Röttger Stirnberg and Catharina Balthes zu Reiste, married couple, declare that they will bequeath their Balthes dwelling with living and dead inventory to the honorable and virtuous Elisabeth Fred
2 CONC ebolinges for many years of loyal service. They ask Hermann and Toniesen Lomann, father and son, Everhardt Schulte zu Landenbeck, the judge zu Eslohe and Reiste Jacob Scheffer to sign and seal the letter of purchase. Signatures: J
2 CONC acobus Scheffer, Caspar (Stirnberg gt.) Baltz, for me and my housewives, Hermann Lomann, magistrate, Ebert Schulte (from Landenbeck), '''I confess Tonies Lohmann to me and Catrina my married housewife that this is true'''. (Origin
2 CONC al certificate at the Lohof),
2 CONT
