1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Heidenreich VII. 'der Altere'  von Plettenberg, Herr zu Bamenohl,''' born around 1405 (religion: rK ), died after 1478, urk. 1426-1478.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''To Bamenohl, 1397-1466, Gem. Angela von Heggen, line to Bamenohl). The line to Bamenohl died out in 1680'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Guntran v. Plettenberg, son of the departed Heidenreich, ....."
2 CONT
2 CONT Events:
2 CONT
2 CONT • '''Notarized, 1397-1466'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Fact: '''Acquired the Bamenohl estate''', 1440, Bamenohl, NW, DEU.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Notarized, 1466-1497.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Notarized, 17 Jul 1469. '''Heydenrich, Herman, Gunterman and Hinrich''', sons of the late '''Hinrich van''' Plettenberch, declare a dispute about the 5 marks from the tithe to Vailbricht, which were prescribed to their '''grandf
2 CONC ather Hinrich van Plettenberch''', and about the dispute with the Ewich monastery that they had been satisfied by the knight Johan van Haitzvelt and his brother Junker Johan. They deliver their documents to the monastery. Siegel H
2 CONC ermans van Plettenbracht and Goderts Refflinchusen, Gografen zu Attendorn Witnesses: Hinrich Schaner, waiter zu Arnesborch, Evert van den Broke, Engelbert van Plettenberch, Wilhem Vaget. In the sancti Allexii confessoris Notes: Ur
2 CONC schr., Pgt., 2 seals attached: 1) Herm. v. Plettenberg; 2) Godert Refflinchusen (like 1463 Febr. 24)
2 CONT
2 CONT Heidenreich married Angela VON HEYGEN, daughter of Wedekind VON HEYGEN zu Ewig, Knappe and Meene (Katharina?). (Angela VON HEYGEN was born before 1438.)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Plettenberg-Bamenohl line (expired)''':
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Plettenberg-Bamenohl line''' goes back to''' Heidenreich von Plettenberg'''. Possibly he was a son of Hunold II. In 1341 he bought the bailiwick in Plettenberg and was married to''' Elisabeth von Altena''' . '''Heidenrich i
2 CONC s also the progenitor of the Lenhausen-Stockum tribe.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Both''' son Heidenreich''' (* around 1402, † around 1474) was a '''squire and heir of the Finnentrop castle complex''', today Altfinnentrop. '''Around 1433 he married the heiress Angela von Heyen (Heygen) and thus came into joint 
2 CONC ownership of the Bamenohl house''' . In 1447 he was able to expand his holdings at Bamenohl. Bamenohl later came into the possession of the Plettenberg-Heeren line (see above)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
