2 CONT Lichtenstein, H, ''Travels in Southern Africa'', mentions him (on page 168 of vol I) meeting with their party in 1804, at the farm of his son-in-law, Jacobus du Preez, near the Krombek and Vet rivers between Swellendam and Riversd
2 CONC ale. He says that he was a member of Van Reenen's party that travelled to the Eastern Cape to search from the Grosvenor survivors in 1790-1. He also mentions the existence of an organ in a room on the farm 'appropriated for divine
2 CONC  service', and that one of the Muller daughters played it very well. The organ was built by a Cape Town craftsman by the name of Hoddersum.
