1 NAME William M /Dueweke/
2 GIVN William M
2 SURN Dueweke
2 _MARNM Dueweke
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Anchorville
3 STAE MI
1 BIRT
2 DATE 7 JUL 1866
2 ADDR
3 CITY Detroit
3 STAE Michigan
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 JUN 1945
2 ADDR
3 CITY Anchorville at Home
3 STAE Michigan
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Flour and Feed Dealer, Mechanic
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Dueweke and first wife, Christine, were the children of siblings.  Thus they were first cousins.  They received dispensation from the Catholic Church in order to be married.  This was related by William's d
2 CONC aughter, Bernadine, to Karen Dueweke, William's granddaughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married by J. F. Friedland, Pastor. Witnesses: Alex Lauhoff and Mine Lauhoff. Marriage of first cousins was and is still illegal in Michigan.
2 CONT
2 CONT The June 1900 Census records William as living at 225 corrected to 244 Russell St. (Was the numbering system changed that caused that correction?  All addresses on that document have been corrected.), widowed and living with daugh
2 CONC ters Stella and Alice, brother Frank, 24, and sister, Ann, 28.  Missing from this address is new baby, Arthur, born Jan, 12, 1900.  This birth incurred the death of wife, Christine, causing the 'widowed' status.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE concerning his middle name (by Uwe Deininghaus):
2 CONT
2 CONT There is one document giving a hint what his middle name M stands for:
2 CONT
2 CONT Please take a look at the marriage affidavit of William Dueweke with his first wife, Christina Lauhoff:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:939K-253D-T6?i=1252&amp...
2 CONT
2 CONT On the top, he writes an N. (instead of M.) as middle name, but when you come to the signature on the bottom, it reads "William Math[e]w Dueweke".
2 CONT
2 CONT So the M probably stands for Mathew. If he had been born in Germany, his given name would read Wilhelm Matthias (as his father's given name was Wilhelm Ludwig).
