1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Andrew Brinkman Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Joseph Brinkman, passed away January 30, 2011, while on vacation. He was born January 29, 1931, in Detroit. He was a member of St. Edmunds Catholic Church, Knights of Columbus, he was a Korean War Veteran and P.O.W. Andrew 
2 CONC was retired from Chrysler as a Software Engineer after more than 30 years. He had a bachelors degree in Computer Science. Mr. Brinkman enjoyed socializing, playing cards, sports and traveling. He is survived by his wife, Rosemary.
2 CONC  Children, Joseph (Linda) and William. Step father of Daniel Dennis, Dawn (Gary) Schumer, Holly Dennis and daughter-in-law, Christine Brinkman. Grandfather of 14; great-grandfather of 3. Brother of Marilyn (Joseph) Schnieder and V
2 CONC irginia Ann Porzandek. Predeceased by wife, Carolyn Brinkman in 1989; daughter, Marianne Brinkman in 2004; and sister, Marie Jean Sloan. Visitation Friday 2 -8 p.m. with a 7 p.m. Rosary followed by Knights of Columbus Service at B
2 CONC uehler Funeral Home, 26429 Gratiot, Roseville. Instate Saturday, 9:30 a.m. until time of 10 a.m. Service at St. Edmunds Catholic Church, 14025 Twelve Mile, Warren. Interment will be in Resurrection Cemetery.
2 CONT Published by The Macomb Daily on Feb. 9, 2011.
