2 CONC  his Waldenburg castle fiefdom; '''in 1313 the advocatus de Heygen carries goods in Heygen''' and the right to a meal in Ahausen as a fiefdom from Count Wilhelm von Arnsberg; In 1325 '''Herberd von Heyen''' was a witness when the 
2 CONC Grafschaft monastery transferred its rights to the main courtyard in Attendorn to the city of Attendorn, in 1326 '''Herbordus advocatus de Heygen, miles(knight), appeared as a witness for the knight Theodor von Schnellenberg,''' i
2 CONC n 1331 the list of feudal men of the Count Konrad von Dortmund as not enfeoffed on: Herbord Voghet to Heyen and Herman syn broder; In 1338 the advocate in Heygen is listed in the fiefdom register of Count Gottfried IV von Arnsberg
2 CONC  with a farm, fishing and meal rights in Heygen. son ofN von Heygen.
