1 NOTE {geni:about_me} • Fact: '''Ritter und Herr zu Hundem. ''' • Beurkundet, 26 Feb 1307. 1307.II.26 '''Denhardus miles dictus de Humene''' (soll Hundeme heißen), seine Gemahlin''' Felicitas''' und '''seine Söhne Denhardus, Godefridus 
2 CONC und Johannes''' entsagen zu Gunsten des Deutschen Hauses zu Marburg ihren Ansprüchen auf den Hof in Anzefahr. (i.b. II No. 113) Auf der Rückseite der Urkunde steht von der Hand Bruder Konrads: Composito inter frates et Deinhardus 
2 CONC de Hundeme. Das Siegel Deinhards ist dreieckig und führt einen rechtsschreitenden Fuchs.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.isphording.info/html/genealogie/maindatabase02/9002.html
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Degenhard(Denhard) von Hundem(von Bruch), Herr zu Hundem''', born around 1290 (religion: rK ), died after 1332, urk. 1307-1332, 1362 dead, son of''' Degenhard(Denhard) von Anzefahr(von Hundem) and Felicitas N.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Luitgard von Bicken''', born around 1300 (religion: rK ), died after 1362, urk. 1362, daughter of '''Konrad von Bicken.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT From this marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. 	'''Wiedekind von Hundem''', born around 1320 (religion: rK ), died after 1369, urk. 1362-1369, 1412 dead, Herman van Ole, Wilhelm's son, and the brothers Johan and Degenhart van Hundeme vouch for a sale in 1369 and promise sto
2 CONC rage in Vredeberg if necessary, Wydekint van Hundeme confesses that the aforementioned was made by his brother Johan van Hundeme Sale has taken place with his consent. Married to''' Bela von Leyssen (Krevet),''' born around 1320 (
2 CONC religion: rK ), died after 1419, [or Bela von Wedinghausen, Heidenreich's daughter] urk. 1419 Wwe. Daughter of Menke von Leyssen (Kreweit)  .
2 CONT 2. 	'''Degenhard von Hundem''', born around 1322 (religion: rK ), died after 1373 , urk. 1356-1373, in 1373 renounces his claims to the tithe and court in Modenbeke (Maumke, municipality of Förde), which his brother Johannes van H
2 CONC undme has transferred to him, towards Rotger van Osterndorp.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. 	'''Adolf von Hundem (Bruch) , born around 1325'''. 4th 	Johann von Hundem (von dem Broyke) , born around 1327 (religion: rK ), died after 1369 , urk. 1362-1369 Herman van Ole, Wilhelm's son, and the brothers Johan and Degenhar
2 CONC t van Hundeme vouch for the aforementioned sale and promise storage in Vredeberg, if necessary, Wydekint van Hundeme confesses that the aforementioned sale made by his brother Johan van Hundeme with his consent is done.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Degenhard von Hundem gt. von (dem) Bruch, Ritter 1300–1325, x
2 CONT
2 CONT • Notarized, 26 Feb 1307. 1307.II.26 Denhardus miles dictus de Humene (should be called Hundeme), his wife '''Felicitas and his sons Denhardus, Godefridus and Johannes''' renounce their claims to the court in Anzefahr in favor of 
2 CONC the German House of Marburg. (ib II No. 113) On the back of the document is written by Brother Konrad's hand: Composito inter frates et Deinhardus de Hundeme. Deinhard's seal is triangular and shows a right-striding fox.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
