1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Widekind von Hundem gt. von (dem) Bruch''', 1335–Haus Bruch, 1412, x
2 CONT
2 CONT • Notarized, 22 Feb 1369. Herman van Ole, Wilhelm's son, and the brothers Johan and Degenhart van Hundeme vouch for the aforementioned sale and promise storage in Vredeberg if necessary.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Wydekint van Hundeme acknowledges that the aforementioned sale made by his brother Johan van Hundeme''' was made with his consent.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Notarized, 14 Sep 1375. Johann von Hundeme, called von dem Bruche Wegelung, gives the Keppel monastery a grain pension from his estate in Wurdinkhusen in the parish of Hundeme to equip his daughter, his brother Alph and his, his
2 CONC  brother and his parents Memorie.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Notarized, 25 Mar 1412. '''Johan van Hundem''', called van dem Broycke, the''' deceased Wedekind's son''', notarized that, with the consent of his mother, brother and sister, he gave his own to Johan van Ole, who lives in Bylste
2 CONC n, for 9 Rhenish guilders Fyghen, Kunnen's daughter sold in the Resypes. The seal of the exhibitor, the '''brothers Rothger''' and '''Wyllem van Leysen''', called Creuete, to Pressel, damaged.
2 CONT
2 CONT Widekind married '''Bele VON LEISSE gt. Krevet, daughter of Rotger v.Leysen gt. KREVET''' and Unknown, circa 1385. ('''Bele VON LEISSE gt. Kreve'''t was born about '''1363 in Hengstebeck''' and died after '''1419 in Bilstein''', N
2 CONC W, DEU.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
