1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Franz Lüning(von Luininck), Lord of Wittenstein and Schlichthorst.''' Bremischer Field Marshall in Schmalkaldischen war 1546/47. Droste (Marshall, official, chamberlain, person in charge) at Ravensburg. 1551 app
2 CONC ointed as Droste for Fürstenau. In 1554 he was appointed Droste for Fürstenau and Vörden.1556 purchaser of property (Gut=estate, farm) Schlichthorst. 1557purchased Wielage and inheritor of Bokel and Talge. 1559 purchaser  from Gra
2 CONC f von Tecklenburg: Frei-gericht (free court) of Englenen andGogericht of Schwagsdorf. 1569 Schlichthorst manor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation help from Luise Schaub (Zerbe). Franz was governor at Fürstenau and Vörden, Hunteburg, Lord at Wittenstein and Schlichthorst. He wanted to be involved in politics and had to have alarge land holding to be called to the
2 CONC  legislature. Therefore, he purchased the estate of Schlichthorst which enabled him to be alegislator in 1569. He gave his Lordship good advice, but had to help out when a mortgage granted by the Duke to the city of Antwerpen(Holl
2 CONC and) went bad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: '''One natural son Martin Lüning. other children by Helene zu Hünfeld und Ippenburg von dem Busshe: Diedrich, Albrecht (Albert), Anna, and Jürgen.'''
