1 NAME Cornelis /Rademeyer/
2 GIVN Cornelis
2 SURN Rademeyer
2 _MARNM Rademeyer
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 3 SEP 1766
2 PLAC Swellendam, Cape, South Africa
2 ADDR
1 BAPM
2 DATE 1 MAR 1767
2 PLAC Kaapstad Nederduitse Gereformeerde Kerk
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cape Town
3 STAE Western Cape
3 CTRY South Africa
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 APR 1843
2 ADDR
3 CITY Tsitsikama
3 STAE Eastern Cape
3 CTRY South Africa
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} RADEMEYER Jacobus
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacobus RADEMEYER van Weeze in Kleef, Duitsland, het as soldaat met die skip Schakenbosch in 1751 in Tafelbaai geland. Voordat Rademeyer in 1767 burgerskap verkry het, was hy vir ses jaar, van 1754 tot 1760, waarnemende landdros v
2 CONC an Swellendam. Op 26 Maart 1756 het hy met Anna Margaretha CLAASEN in die huwelik getree.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hulle vyf kinders was:
2 CONT * (1) Jacobus Coenraad (1757), burger van Stellenbosch en getroud 31 Oktober 1779 met Regina VAN ZYL, die weduwee van Gideon DE JAGER; hertroud 26 Julie 1784 met Anna Maria VIVIER, die weduwee van Pieter OOSTHUIZEN; 6 kinders.
2 CONT * (2) Isabella Elisabeth (1759), getroud met Johan Christiaan KRIEK.
2 CONT * (3) Nicolaas (1762).
2 CONT * (4) Aletta (1764), getroud met Hendrik VAN DER WAT.
2 CONT * ('''5) Cornelis (1767), burger van Swellendam en getroud 19 April 1789 met Hester FERREIRA hertroud 12 Junie 1791 met Jacoba FERREIRA; 12 kinders.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Bronne: “Die AFRIKANER FAMILIENAAMBOEK & PERSONALIA” (1955) saamgestel deur J.H Redelinghuys
2 CONT
2 CONT Bydrae: Pieter Conradie pietc@iafrica.com
2 CONT
2 CONT - http://www.stamouers.com/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=411:rademeyer-jacobus-&catid=6:r-u&Itemid=36
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LCCQ-J9S
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Rademeijer-29
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelis Rademeyer was the field-cornet of the Langkloof area at the time that Commissioner-General JA Uitenhage de Mist and his party, including Hinrich Lichtenstein, travelled through the Southern Cape in 1804/5. They stayed at 
2 CONC his farm in January 1805, having been at his father-in-law, Stephanus Ferreira's, farm before that. Cornelis acted as the party's guide in the eastern section of the Longkloof. Lichtenstein, H, ''Travels in Southern Africa'', 1812
2 CONC , London, Vol I, page 213-4.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT FERREIRA FAMILIE - FAMILY
2 CONT Eerste Uitgawe - First Edition
2 CONT April 1998
2 CONT Janet Melville & Emmarentia S Ferreira
2 CONT Redakteur - Gideon de V de Kock - Editor
