0 @N6000000003811537771@ NOTE Last Will giving names of children TRANSLATION OF THE LAST WILL & TESTAMENT OF ANOHONY MICHAEL MULLER & MARIA POTGIETER
1 CONT
1 CONT L.rs B. No 19 This day the 5 th April 1816 before Charles Allen Secretary of the District of Utenhage and acting as Notary in the presence of the latter named witnesses citizen ANTHONY MICHAEL MULLER and the housewife MARIA POTGIE
1 CONC TER, real persons and my secretary and known witnesses declare that they of sound body and mind and fully able to pass this matter and to give notice of their wishes of the disposal of their goods in the event of their deaths and 
1 CONC declare that this is done on their own initiative without induction or persecution of anyone recalling all Testament Codicils and other acts of ultimate wills both communicated or expressed individually before this date not wishin
1 CONC g that same be of any power or value but to the contrary to be of no value and to be envisaged as such  - to this effect the testators declare and legate that before the death of the longest living to leave to their children their
1 CONC  place of residence, to Cornelius Johannes and Johannes Muller the farm named Welbedagt situated in the field corner area Zwartkops River District Uitenhage for the sum of Three Thousand Ryx Dollars, furthermore the testators of t
1 CONC he longest living of them both can book from the estate a male or female slave for the sum of Five Hundred Ryx Dollars and eventually when marring or reaching adult years their children will each receive the sum of Sixty Ryx Dolla
1 CONC rs to be used as a dowry (wedding gift).
1 CONT
1 CONT Now to continue to the election of executors the testators declare reciprocally that the first executors will be the longest living of them both and nominate to institute that all goods without exception both movable and immovable
1 CONC  not excluding anything in the world to accept as free and own goods and to possess everything with the understanding that the longest living will remain responsible to see to it that children already born from this marriage and p
1 CONC ossible further children will receive an honest and Christian upbringing and maintain them until they reach the age of majority or prior marriage or other approved state when each of the father or mother will have to provide proof
1 CONC  about the state of the legacy in case the longest living eventually legitimately may be forced in the case of re-marriage to publicize the entire estate to find the provisions to payout itself, although the testators expressly wi
1 CONC sh that the longest living should remain in full and undisturbed possession of the estate to provide for the use and maintenance and education of the minors but in case the testators should die without leaving any children the tes
1 CONC tator declares that his father Cornelius Johannes Muller senior in the legitimate portion, fathers and the legacy of their children competing in rights, the testatrix declares that she has no living parents any more. The testators
1 CONC  nominate the longest living of them as executor or executrix of this will as well as Cornelius Johannes Muller and Gert van Rooyen as distributors of the estate on behalf of minor legacies with power to assume and surrogate in or
1 CONC der that  else will intervene with the minor legacies, such as officials or Magistrates who would wish to ex-officio or otherwise get involved and in particular the "Hererden Weesmeesteren" (orphan chamber) at the Cape of Good Hop
1 CONC e not withstanding my pre-advertisement or otherwise as it is difficult to turn down politely in this manner. Lastly the testators reserve the right and ability to add further bequests at the foot of this document either by a sepa
1 CONC rate act  or other bequests and apart from the legacy contained in this will to dispose of other goods as becomes necessary from time to time and that clauses added to this effect will have the same power and value as if it were i
1 CONC ncluded in this will. All the above having been explained to the testators who declare that they clearly understand this to be their last Will and Testament and that it will therefore be valid and take place as a Solem Will as wel
1 CONC l as any codicil gifts in the case of death or according to rights which may exist in spite of any omissions of solemnity which may be insinuated but binding on one or other rights of the beneficiaries.
1 CONT
1 CONT Attended at the Secretariat of Uitenhage on the abovementioned date in presence of the clerk Adriaan De Waal and the messenger Johannes ________ as witness and the testators and my Secretary properly signed on _______
1 CONT
1 CONT Quo Attestor Chas Allen
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT CODICIL ATTACHED
1 CONT
1 CONT On this day 30 January 1830
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Empowered by the reserved clause in the previous will attached to this document we the undersigned Anthony Michael Muller and Maria Potgieter real people have agreed to make the following alterations namely our placed of residence
1 CONC  Welbedaght situated in the field country of Swartkops River district of Uitenhauge (now Port Elizabeth) to bequeath to our sons Cornelius Johannis, Anthony Michael, Johannis,  Ignatius Theodorus, Petrus Hendrik, Hilgert Isaac Abr
1 CONC aham and Stefhanus Muller for the sum of Four Thousand Cape Ryx Dollars, after the deceased of the longest living of us, to be realised by the abovementioned sumsthat is a sum Five hundred Cape Ryx Dollars each on the understandin
1 CONC g never the less that our son Petrus Hendrik be excluded from realising the above amount or any portion of thereof as a legacy in this willthe sum of Five Hundred Ryx Dollars.
1 CONT
1 CONT Furthermore we declare that any of our sons be inclined to sell the portion of the farm belonging to him he would not sell to a stranger but only to one of this brothers for the sum of Five Hundred Ryx Dollars. And if in our time 
1 CONC one of our sons would die each of the remaining would enjoy a larger and equal share, nevertheless the abovementioned value of Four Thousand Cape Ryx Dollars may not be reduced.
1 CONT
1 CONT In respect of the funds we desire when we are both deceased, and the nominated sons hereby have put these funds in the general legacy, this should be split into two equal portions, one half to be shared by our daughters Susanna El
1 CONC izabeth, Maria Jacoba Muller and the other half to be equally and jointly shared by the children
1 CONT
1 CONT This done on the date and year as above on the farm Welbedaght and the Bakens River in the presence of
1 CONT
1 CONT ______________ S Hartman
1 CONT
1 CONT ______________ J W Botha
1 CONT
1 CONT ______________ Thenius Renny     AM MULLER
1 CONT
1 CONT ______________ C G Hartman     M POTGIETER
1 CONT
1 CONT ______________ J P van Niekerk
1 CONT
1 CONT ______________ Petrus Prinsloo
1 CONT
1 CONT ______________ G H Holtshausen
